From ea3f2dc9a13daed099bc37e72d3f4016c4d6203d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:39:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Fix compile breaks the 2026-11-10 upstream merge left outside
 conflict markers

Upstream changed three interfaces that fork-only code still used the old shape of, none flagged by git:

- common_prompt_checkpoint::data_tgt/data_dft are now common_state_data (no-init allocator vector); the server's captured-checkpoint, slot-save and prompt-cache-spill paths still passed std::vector<uint8_t>.
- common_get_device_memory_data_impl takes paths_model and hp_nsk; the fork's common_get_device_memory_data_with_extra (split-balance probe) still took a single path.
- the new Clover MoE model calls build_conv_state expecting the concatenated tensor; the fork's build_conv_state returns {prefix, new_tokens} for ggml_ssm_conv_split, so clover-moe now uses that, like qwen35/qwen3next.

Vulkan+RPC build with tests now links clean.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
